it><patcit ucid="JP-53125299-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>53125299</doc-number><kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="JP-61036116-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>61036116</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X"  name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-6198164-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>6198164</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7144128-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7144128</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7213910-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7213910</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9012540-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9012540</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1129774A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA NORIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KANAZAWA TAKAAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOYOTA MOTOR CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA, NORIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANAZAWA, TAKAAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOYOTA JIDOSHA KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA NORIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KANAZAWA TAKAAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA, NORIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANAZAWA, TAKAAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An adsorbent for hydrocarbon (HC) comprising a zeolite which contains none of monovalent metal elements and has an SiO2/Al2O3 molar ratio of 100 or higher and an average primary particle size of 1  mu m or less. The adsorbent exhibits high adsorptivity for HC even after a durability test due to the absence of a monovalent metal element such as Na and, due to its small average primary particle size, have a large surface area for adsorbing HC and thus shows an increased amount of HC adsorbed relative to its weight. An adsorbent for HC comprising a first zeolite which comprises at least one of ZSM-5 and ferrierite and has an SiO2/Al2O3 molar ratio of 100 or lower, and carries at least one of Ag and Pd thereon, and a second zeolite which comprises Y type zeolite having an SiO2/Al2O3 molar ratio of 200 or higher is also disclosed. This adsorbent can efficiently adsorb both lower and higher HC. A catalyst for exhaust gas purification prepared by combining the above-mentioned adsorbent and an oxidizing catalyst exhibits a high percentage of purification with respect to HC in an exhaust gas.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un adsorbant pour hydrocarbure (HC) comprenant une zéolithe ne contenant aucun élément métallique monovalent et présentant un rapport molaire SiO2/Al2O3 supérieur ou égal à 100, et une dimension moyenne de particules élémentaires inférieure ou égale à 1  mu m. Cet agent adsorbant présente un pouvoir adsorbant élevé vis-à-vis des hydrocarbures, même après un essai de durabilité, en raison de l'absence d'élément métallique monovalent tel que Na, et en raison de sa faible dimension moyenne de particules. Cet agent adsorbant présente une grande surface efficace pour l'adsorption des hydrocarbures, et permet par conséquent d'adsorber une quantité d'hydrocarbures accrue par rapport à son poids. L'invention concerne également un agent adsorbant comprenant une première zéolithe contenant au moins une ZMS-5 et une ferriérite, et présente un rapport molaire SiO2/Al2O3 inférieur ou égal à 100, comportant au moins de l'Ag et du Pd, ainsi qu'une deuxième zéolithe contenant une zéolithe de type Y présentant un rapport molaire SiO2/Al2O3 supérieur ou égal à 200. Cet agent adsorbant peut adsorber aussi efficacement des hydrocarbures à haut poids moléculaire que des hydrocarbures à bas poids moléculaire. L'invention concerne en outre un catalyseur pour la purification de gaz d'échappement, préparé par combinaison de l'adsorbant mentionné ci-dessus et d'un catalyseur d'oxydation, ledit catalyseur présentant un taux élevé de purification par rapport aux hydrocarbures présents dans les gaz d'échappement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>